{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"GATE FAIL\n\n**A — Blocking**\n\n- **C9 can accept the wrong base deterministically.** In a G4b replay, q01 published $430–460B after adjusting its subtotal. q22 still used the old $400–435B subtotal, and both checks passed. Require q22 to use the published forecast, or the corresponding calculation behind each scenario when the published answer is a range summary. [C9 base selection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:585)\n- **The recomputed amount governs C6 alone.** An R2z2 replay approved a payload that still stated $49.91B on the rung starting at $50B. In R1, C3 approved two declared $127.1B quarters even though recomputation put Data Center at $127.247B and the whole company at $127.120B. Use one recomputed result for checks and for the amount approved for publication. [C6 band check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:480) · [C3 comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:554)\n\n**B — Non-blocking.** No relabelling findings."}}
